          </p>

          <p>
            Notice too that none of the wireless stations list a big total. Wireless charging is limited by the standard, not by the brick behind it, so a wireless pad will never charge a phone as fast as a good USB-C cable. That is fine on a nightstand where the phone has eight hours, and frustrating on a kitchen counter where it has twenty minutes. Many households end up with one of each, and that is a sensible split rather than a waste.
          </p>
