        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy a charging station for the place it will live. A nightstand wants a wireless 3-in-1 with certified MagSafe or Qi2; a desk wants enough USB-C wattage on one port for the laptop; a family counter wants enough ports that nobody steals a cable. Read the per-port numbers, not the total, and pair the station with cables rated for the job.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then think one step further. A drop zone where every device charges each night is the easiest outage plan you will ever make, as long as a power station or power bank is charged and ready to keep it running when the grid goes down.
          </p>
